{"id":45752,"ord":92,"n_segments":146,"prev":45751,"next":45753,"doc":{"id":"56679","title":"56679_Arthur Briggs oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Arthur Briggs","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/56679/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=56679"},"chapter":"Paris, the Blackbirds and Noble Sissle","title":"The Smith Brothers as trumpeters","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Briggs comments on Russell Smith's tone, too light to lead a dance orchestra, and on the three Smith brothers.","period":null,"year_from":null,"year_to":null,"words":170,"start":[232,12],"end":[234,12],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=56679#s45752","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Russell Smith","qid":"Q2176953","n":3},{"name":"Joe Smith","qid":"Q5475919","n":1},{"name":"Luke Smith","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Smith Brothers","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":35,"theme_name":"Remembering the early trumpeters and their styles","community":77,"community_name":"Trumpeters I admired: rating the horn players","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":232,"b":12,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Well, okay, Joe Smith, then was a good reader?"},{"p":232,"b":13,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Right. Very good."},{"p":232,"b":14,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Good high register?"},{"p":233,"b":0,"s":"","x":"Briggs 233"},{"p":233,"b":1,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Yes. The Smith Brothers were three unique brothers as trumpet players."},{"p":233,"b":2,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Well, Russell Smith was more of a first man, right?"},{"p":233,"b":3,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"He was a first man. Russell was not -- he was not really a good balance on the first."},{"p":233,"b":4,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Well --"},{"p":233,"b":5,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"For a dance orchestra."},{"p":233,"b":6,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Why."},{"p":233,"b":7,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Luke, yes. Luke, yes."},{"p":233,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"They say that Russell probably had a little too much of the brass band playing, you see."},{"p":233,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Yes. A little blaring?"},{"p":233,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Yes, yes. Not -- well, I don't know how to explain."},{"p":234,"b":0,"s":"","x":"Briggs"},{"p":234,"b":1,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"A little too heavy-handed."},{"p":234,"b":2,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Too light."},{"p":234,"b":3,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"It would seem too light."},{"p":234,"b":4,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Too light."},{"p":234,"b":5,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Oh, I see."},{"p":234,"b":6,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"It was too light."},{"p":234,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"I see, I see."},{"p":234,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"It was too light, it didn't have the punch."},{"p":234,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"I see, I see."},{"p":234,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"The punch. It's awfully hard for a first trumpet player, because you have to lead your section."},{"p":234,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Right, exactly. Yeh."},{"p":234,"b":12,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Well, okay, that's a little bit off the track. But it's interesting."}]}